Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Train=20mT5=20in=20bf16,=20not=20fp16=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20fp16=20overflows=20to=20NaN=20gradients?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

smoke_mt5 on A100 showed loss=0, grad_norm=nan from step 1, eval_loss=nan,
BLEU=0: mT5's activations overflow fp16's range (Google trained mT5 in bf16).
NLLB's fp16 run was healthy (BLEU 38.95), so precision becomes a per-model
default in MODEL_ZOO (mt5_small->bf16, nllb_600m->fp16), overridable via
TrainConfig.precision / run_training.py --precision; bf16 falls back to fp32
on GPUs without support. Legacy fp16 bool kept so old config files load.
